<title>USA: Bon-Ton Stores in $200 mln finance pact.</title>
<headline>Bon-Ton Stores in $200 mln finance pact.</headline>
<dateline>YORK, Pa. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bon-Ton Stores Inc said it is in a new $200 million financing pact with two financial institutions.</p>
<p>The deals consists of an $11 million term loan and a $189 million revolving credit facility and is fully underwritten, the company said.</p>
<p>The collateral includes inventory and selected fixed assets. The new financing replaces a $142 million facility,</p>
<p>consisting of a $57 million term loan and an $85 million revolving credit agreement, also secured by inventory and fixed assets.</p>
<p>The company did not identify the institutions.</p>
</text>
